From 0b70ec6c988d81607f4afa2ff85ed68f23c58dd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:30:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(controller): persist resumable volume create
 operations

Serialize CreateVolume by logical name, fingerprint the complete request, and persist an operation identity before providers that support resumable creation mutate cloud state.

Split controller and node services so durable state lives on the controller PVC, preserve existing providers without resumable operations, enforce capacity limits using provider-normalized sizes, and keep upstream CDH metadata compatible.

Signed-off-by: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
